Overview
Key participants in this meeting include Rich Pace, Derek Chu, Phil Toy, John Ryan, Anupam Dey, Abdul Sabir, and others. The primary focus is an in-depth introduction to Visual Studio Code (VS Code) as a versatile development environment, emphasizing its workspace capabilities, extension ecosystem, and profile management. Rich Pace leads the demonstration, showcasing how VS Code can streamline file management and editing tasks relevant to network as-code projects.
The discussion highlights the critical role of extensions in enhancing VS Code's functionality, with examples like CSV viewers, Cisco iOS syntax highlighters, and YAML support. The concept of profiles is introduced to manage different project requirements and avoid extension conflicts. Integration with AI tools such as Circuit and Cloud Code is explored, noting current limitations and the potential benefits of tighter integration to improve productivity while adhering to Cisco's data governance policies.
Participants delve into the token-based usage model of AI services, clarifying how token consumption impacts session length and costs. Circuit is noted for its generous token limits but slower response times. The meeting concludes with plans for future sessions on GitHub and version control, encouraging collaboration and resource sharing to enhance learning. Overall, the session provides a comprehensive foundation for using VS Code and associated tools effectively in as-code network environments.


