Profiles in VS Code
Rich explains the use of profiles in VS Code to manage different sets of extensions and configurations for various projects or environments. Profiles help avoid conflicts between extensions and allow synchronization across devices. The analogy of profiles as toolboxes for different jobs is discussed.
Rich Pace describes profiles as customizable sets of extensions tied to specific folders or projects.
John Ryan compares profiles to toolboxes containing the necessary tools for each job.
Phil Toy confirms profiles can prevent extension conflicts and synchronize settings across devices.
